    "report": {
      "summary": "All 48 Teradata scripts are converted to DuckDB. Each one reproduces its legacy output exactly on dataset A on the first attempt, and each has an approved review. The inventory shows 48 passing and 48 approved. The conversions handle Teradata's runtime behaviour with general rules rather than values taken from the data: (1) In session mode, text comparisons ignore letter case and trailing spaces. Every string filter, IN-list and join (including the join from CHAR(10) to VARCHAR sku) compares upper(rtrim(x,' ')) on both sides. (2) With RoundHalfwayMagUp=FALSE, decimal casts round exact halves to the nearest even digit, so they are written as CAST(round_even(x,1) AS DECIMAL(14,1)). (3) TOP n WITH TIES becomes RANK() <= n with DESC NULLS LAST. (4) Teradata puts NULLs first when sorting ascending, so this is written out explicitly in ROW_NUMBER. (5) Whole-number division drops the remainder (rounds toward zero), so it uses DuckDB's // operator. (6) ZEROIFNULL becomes COALESCE. Two pieces of legacy behaviour look wrong but were kept for parity and recorded as legacy_bug: g08 drops the fraction from items-per-order, and g09 ranks unshipped orders first.",
