      "risks": [
        "Case folding uses DuckDB upper(), which follows Unicode. It matches Teradata for ASCII/LATIN data, but non-Latin text could compare differently.",
        "Only spaces are treated as padding. Tabs or other trailing whitespace still make values differ, as in Teradata. Leading spaces are significant in both engines.",
        "Teradata SUM(INTEGER) can fail with an overflow on very large totals, while DuckDB widens to HUGEINT, so the DuckDB job succeeds where the legacy job would fail.",
        "g10 CROSS JOINs etl_control and assumes it has exactly one row. More than one run_date would produce several rows per customer in both engines.",
        "Parity was proven only on dataset A. The rules are written generally, but edge cases that A lacks (for example negative amounts that land exactly on a half) are covered only by reasoning, not by reconciliation."
      ]
    },
